{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread","id":1020797,"title":"The Critical Role Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-22T01:03:26-08:00","id":1020797,"title":"The Critical Role Thread","content":"I was pondering whether one thread would be for nonspoiler discussion and one for Spoilers but well spoilers are intertwined...<br /> <br /> So Critical Role is a broadcast of the weekly D&amp;D game of a bunch of Nerdy Ass Voice Actors with Matt Mercer as the Dungeon Master. It is damn good, Matt Mercer (He was Leon in Resident Evil and a billion other roles), so it also includes Laura Bailey ( the voice of Kid Trunks, Shinchan, Lust from Full Metal Alchemist, and a bunch of Video game roles), Her husband Travis Willingham (He was the voice of Mustang in Full Metal Alchemist, Thor in the Avengers Assemble Cartoon, and a lot of other roles, like a Greaser Robert Duval beat up in 2nd hand Lions).<br /> <br /> Its a great show, you can find it at the Geek and Sundry Website, Twitch TV or Youtube. <br /> <a href=\"http://geekandsundry.com/shows/critical-role/\" target=\"_blank\">http://geekandsundry.com/shows/critical-role/</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL7atuZxmT954bCkC062rKwXTvJtcqFB8i\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/playlist?lis...rKwXTvJtcqFB8i</a><br /> <br /> Its a fun show and long running. And while I wish it was a whitewolf game they are playing Matt Mercer is a brilliant and skilled game master and brings a lot of quick thinking and system fidelity to the table. They break the fourth wall a lot, but they also have emotional scenes, and they have fantastic fan art! Go and watch it!! I finally caught up!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><b>So without Further ado the Spoilery Discussions lie ahead!</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:72px\">SPOILER DISCUSSIONS!!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I caught up! I'm sad Tiberius isn't with the party anymore actually, him and Grog had the most interesting in character moments!<br /> <br /> Big question! Anyone else feel Taliesin Jaffe cheats? Maybe not intentionally but his friggin metal dice are not balanced, all the other guys at the table notice and comment on it, he regularly rolls natural twenties, sometimes like 5+ a night! Others commented he had a high roll when he rolled another dice set, but that does nothing to make me think he doesn't cheat...<br /> <br /> I also think Wil Wheaton cheats, I believe he purposely tries to make it seem like he rolls impossibly poorly as a showman trick....<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides that I think it would be fun to have the Vox Machina party in an Exalted game as a bunch of Fairfolk or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> I never really read D&amp;D so I only get the jist of the rules and the setting. So like a rating of 10 is average human in a trait? What is the in character explanation for the party after killing some goblins all of the sudden they know more spells and can cook or whatever. It feels to much like a videogame, I don't understand how powers even work in D&amp;D, most things are spells? I don't get how for instance Vex learns new ranger powers? Some people in the world just randomly have magic powers in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> They also seem to ignore that Tiberius had excellent Charisma, he shouldn't have been treated so much like a goof, and Percy tries to be a world class genius, but he chooses battle stats like Dexterity over Intelligence or Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T01:37:21-08:00","id":1040492,"title":"","content":"Surprised to see this lacking responses! I'm an avid fan; I watch the show proper and the aftershow every week. I think it's great stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a fun show and long running. And while I wish it was a whitewolf game they are playing Matt Mercer is a brilliant and skilled game master and brings a lot of quick thinking and system fidelity to the table. They break the fourth wall a lot, but they also have emotional scenes, and they have fantastic fan art! Go and watch it!! I finally caught up! </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that Taliesin Jaffe is an old-school VtM and WtA player, who has expressed interest several times in running a one-shot for the rest of the group once he familiarises himself with V20 rules: so you might get your wish after all there ;D I personally think the group might enjoy Changeling or something else instead, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Big question! Anyone else feel Taliesin Jaffe cheats? </div> </div> </div>Matt has said before (I think on twitter? Maybe on the subreddit...I could find it if I looked) that the only player who cheats 'is no longer at the table', i.e it was Orion, and he has actually made Tal switch out his dice before. I think it's just luck + the fact that everyone pays more attention to his nat 20s than anyone else's, since they expect him to have them. Confirmation bias is a hell of a thing. I do recall an instance in the Feywild arc where Taliesin rolled with Marisha's dice after she'd rolled several 1s in quick succession, though...and rolled a 20 with them. He's not cheating; I think he's just a witch. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They also seem to ignore that Tiberius had excellent Charisma, he shouldn't have been treated so much like a goof, and Percy tries to be a world class genius, but he chooses battle stats like Dexterity over Intelligence or Wisdom. </div> </div> </div>I think it's a consequence of each class having certain dump stats more than anything. Tibs was a sorcerer, so he needed high Charisma, but he never really felt like he <i>should</i> have it. I still think he would have been better as a Wizard. Still, I have a sorcerer with 18 Cha in my PF game, and he's also an awkward creature. Percy is more interesting: iirc Taliesin has said that Percy is a man who <i>thinks</i> he is a genius, but is very much not, making that stat choice more acceptable imo. [VAGUE SPOILERS] You recall that his hubris here came back to bite him in the end. But a lot of this comes down to the relative lack of customisation one can do in 5e/PF. <br /> <br /> Anyway! Apologies for bumping, but I do love this silly show. Worth a watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12920-anomalocaris","name":"anomalocaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:10:34-08:00","id":1041707,"title":"","content":"I only recently discovered the show and I am binge watching it to catch up (last episode I saw was the 60th, the first with a live audience) I love it to pieces. <br /> <br /> How do you wanna do this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:50:48-08:00","id":1041918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1041707#post1041707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only recently discovered the show and I am binge watching it to catch up (last episode I saw was the 60th, the first with a live audience) I love it to pieces. <br /> <br /> How do you wanna do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, though I'm not quite that far in yet. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> for recommending it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:28:27-08:00","id":1042076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>anomalocaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1040492#post1040492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised to see this lacking responses! I'm an avid fan; I watch the show proper and the aftershow every week. I think it's great stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Worth noting that Taliesin Jaffe is an old-school VtM and WtA player, who has expressed interest several times in running a one-shot for the rest of the group once he familiarises himself with V20 rules: so you might get your wish after all there ;D I personally think the group might enjoy Changeling or something else instead, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Matt has said before (I think on twitter? Maybe on the subreddit...I could find it if I looked) that the only player who cheats 'is no longer at the table', i.e it was Orion, and he has actually made Tal switch out his dice before. I think it's just luck + the fact that everyone pays more attention to his nat 20s than anyone else's, since they expect him to have them. Confirmation bias is a hell of a thing. I do recall an instance in the Feywild arc where Taliesin rolled with Marisha's dice after she'd rolled several 1s in quick succession, though...and rolled a 20 with them. He's not cheating; I think he's just a witch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's a consequence of each class having certain dump stats more than anything. Tibs was a sorcerer, so he needed high Charisma, but he never really felt like he <i>should</i> have it. I still think he would have been better as a Wizard. Still, I have a sorcerer with 18 Cha in my PF game, and he's also an awkward creature. Percy is more interesting: iirc Taliesin has said that Percy is a man who <i>thinks</i> he is a genius, but is very much not, making that stat choice more acceptable imo. [VAGUE SPOILERS] You recall that his hubris here came back to bite him in the end. But a lot of this comes down to the relative lack of customisation one can do in 5e/PF.<br /> <br /> Anyway! Apologies for bumping, but I do love this silly show. Worth a watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard people site that quote before but I never recall Orion Cheating, and considering how much they put up with Taliesin I don't think it had anything to do with him leaving, from my understanding it had to do with him Blowing up on a fan's deviant art pic.<br /> <br /> But I don't see how him rolling a twenty with Marisha's dice at all absolves him. He flat out shouldn't be allowed to roll his &quot;Golden Snitch&quot; anymore, I mean come on its a metal engraved die, they wouldn't allow that in Vegas or a back alley craps game.<br /> <br /> But yeah a couple weeks ago Matt Mercer mentioned Exalted, meaning he has at least heard of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:22:39-08:00","id":1042151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1042076#post1042076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard people site that quote before but I never recall Orion Cheating, and considering how much they put up with Taliesin I don't think it had anything to do with him leaving, from my understanding it had to do with him Blowing up on a fan's deviant art pic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right; though Matt later said Orion was prone to cheating--he would apparently hide rolls from other players and say they were a few numbers higher than they actually were--he wasn't kicked for that. IIRC it was for going off at a fan who wanted to send him a shirt design, or something? I think Orion mistakenly believed fans were making money off 'his' intellectual property. It was never really discussed outright. I feel sorry for the guy, but eh. Group dynamics have improved since he left.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But I don't see how him rolling a twenty with Marisha's dice at all absolves him. He flat out shouldn't be allowed to roll his &quot;Golden Snitch&quot; anymore, I mean come on its a metal engraved die, they wouldn't allow that in Vegas or a back alley craps game.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> For sure. I <a href=\"http://critrolestats.com/rankings\" target=\"_blank\">checked CRStats</a> just to see what the numbers were: Tal rolls the greatest number of 20s, but Liam and Laura aren't too far behind. Note that they also use metal dice sometimes. The three of them also have comparatively high numbers of nat 1s, though, so part of that is probably just that they're the three who roll most often full stop: they each usually take multiple attacks per round, etc. Anyway! That's enough numbers for lil ol' me today. <br /> <br /> Nice to see some other fans around. I'd be interested to see what other people's favourite episodes are! Mine has been 57, 'Duskmeadow', for a long time: just a perfect little episode imo, with lots of great character development and imagery. I do love how one poor roll (!) on Laura's behalf in 'The Sunken Tomb' has been singehandedly responsible for turning the arcs of a full half of the party in a totally different direction. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12920-anomalocaris","name":"anomalocaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:04:00-08:00","id":1042168,"title":"","content":"Yeah Matt is unforgiving with his traps... hmmm have to think about my favorite eps! Lot of Goodones! I really enjoy the Scanlan Grog dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:10:48-08:00","id":1042291,"title":"","content":"I love Mercer's dwarven swears. And Gilmore and the poor black powder merchant from Vaselheim","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T18:18:54-08:00","id":1175636,"title":"","content":"The first episode of their <a href=\"https://geekandsundry.com/can-you-guess-whos-playing-which-character-in-critical-roles-new-campaign/\" target=\"_blank\">new campaign</a> was last night. I never did manage to catch up on the first campaign, but I'm excited to be able to watch this new one from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I know these are old discussions, but...<br /> Re: Taliesin's high rolls - I don't doubt they're unevenly weighted, but I do doubt he's intentionally cheating. Honestly though, most gaming dice are unevenly weighted, and I personally think that's just kinda part of the game.<br /> Re: Will Wheaton's low rolls - Pure confirmation bias. He makes <i>such</i> a big deal out of it every time he rolls below a 10, brushes it off as an anomaly when he rolls in like the 10-14 range, and turns high rolls into another excuse to point out how unusual it is for him to roll so well. It's also much less entertaining than he seems to think it is. After the second or third time he peaked his mic screaming about how bad his luck was, you could see the exasperation on the rest of the cast's faces, like &quot;ok, we get it, you rolled low. Can we move on please?&quot; Especially Marisha.<br /> Re: Orion's departure - the deviant art thing was definitely the last proverbial straw, but there were bigger issues that they don't generally talk about. He's publicly come out about the fact that he had a serious drug problem at the time, and last I heard he was clean, but understood that he had done too much damage to his relationships with the rest of the cast to be welcome back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T22:26:52-08:00","id":1175694,"title":"","content":"Yeah Orion admitted that he had drug issues and got HIV, that made it extra sad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wish he had his old group of friends, Critical Role gives this group of adults an excellent excuse to hang out with catered food multiple times a week!!!<br /> <br /> It\u2019s exciting having a new set of PCs! Did I miss it or did Travis never get to explain his characters appearance? He\u2019s a burly half orc I get, but I don\u2019t remember him introducing him in the beginning.<br /> <br /> I really like Jester and Gnat the most so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T22:47:00-08:00","id":1175697,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t catch the stream, so I\u2019m going to have to wait for Monday. Very excited to see the new PCs and how they all interact together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T10:38:07-08:00","id":1176000,"title":"","content":"So looking forward to monday.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T12:44:32-08:00","id":1176355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1175636#post1175636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know these are old discussions, but...<br /> Re: Taliesin's high rolls - I don't doubt they're unevenly weighted, but I do doubt he's intentionally cheating. Honestly though, most gaming dice are unevenly weighted, and I personally think that's just kinda part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Critrole stats has various figures and such concerning the numbers of this, that and the other, including percentages vs. averages. (Taliesin *does* roll more 20s, overall, usually than anyone else... but he's also usually making more rolls, on average, than the other PCs usually do as he gets 3 attacks -- sometimes 4-6+, with Action Surge -- per round. Still, while that skews the ratios a bit, last time I checked he still had a statistically disproportionate number of 20s compared to what would be &quot;expected&quot;, so there's that. Similarly, as CRStats determined...)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1175636#post1175636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Will Wheaton's low rolls - Pure confirmation bias. He makes <i>such</i> a big deal out of it every time he rolls below a 10, brushes it off as an anomaly when he rolls in like the 10-14 range, and turns high rolls into another excuse to point out how unusual it is for him to roll so well. It's also much less entertaining than he seems to think it is. After the second or third time he peaked his mic screaming about how bad his luck was, you could see the exasperation on the rest of the cast's faces, like &quot;ok, we get it, you rolled low. Can we move on please?&quot; Especially Marisha.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Wheaton, while only having a much smaller range of rolls to work with (as he only guest'd in two episodes of CR), still rolled disproportionately lower than would be statistically expected overall for his rolls and very much rolled more nat-1s than he &quot;should&quot; have, again per CRStats. So there's *some* legitimacy to his &quot;curse&quot;... lol (Similarly, on other shows he's guested on for G&amp;S, he rolls &quot;badly&quot; for &quot;x&quot;, regardless of the dice/numbers involved -- such as when he played with Matt Mercer, Ivan van Norman and others in a Paranoia game (where low is good and high is bad)... and instead of having disproportionately low rolls (1s, and 1-10s), he rolled high (including several 16-20s, more than he &quot;should&quot; have&quot;... so yeah: there's *something* to the Wheaton Dice Curse(tm)... )<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1175636#post1175636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Orion's departure - the deviant art thing was definitely the last proverbial straw, but there were bigger issues that they don't generally talk about. He's publicly come out about the fact that he had a serious drug problem at the time, and last I heard he was clean, but understood that he had done too much damage to his relationships with the rest of the cast to be welcome back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah -- that was sad/unfortunate. (However, even before the stream had started, Orion had most often been &quot;problematic&quot; and a touch of a pwrgmr in their home-PF game, per Liam's comments and some others. It was manageable, though, and usually not too out of line until the stream got going and Orion's personal issues became... well... <i>issues</i>... ) He and Matt had a friendly-enough encounter a few months ago at some place (with Sam, if I recall correctly), and he/they posted a couple pics of it on Twitter/whatnot, so there's at least a civility in place. (Matt has said at numerous conventions, when the subject of Orion would be brought up, that he genuinely wishes him well and that they are not enemies or anything like that... just sometimes people go on different paths in life and all you can do is wish them well.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh -- apparently (as I just went to check), Orion has taken down all of his Draconian Knights vids/audios/what-have-you, as well as has at least temporarily terminated his Twitch channel, as of a day or two ago. Hope everything is good for him, or at least heading in a good direction... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":". 01-15-2018, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T14:02:30-08:00","id":1176381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1176355#post1176355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Critrole stats has various figures and such concerning the numbers of this, that and the other, including percentages vs. averages. (Taliesin *does* roll more 20s, overall, usually than anyone else... but he's also usually making more rolls, on average, than the other PCs usually do as he gets 3 attacks -- sometimes 4-6+, with Action Surge -- per round. Still, while that skews the ratios a bit, last time I checked he still had a statistically disproportionate number of 20s compared to what would be &amp;quot;expected&amp;quot;, so there's that. Similarly, as CRStats determined...)</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Like I said, I don\u2019t doubt that his dice are unbalanced and favor 20s. I just doubt that this is intentional cheating on Taliesen\u2019s part. Most gaming dice are slightly unbalanced and favor a certain axis, I suspect he has just taken, as many gamers do, to favoring the dice he gets the best results with, rather than knowingly using a loaded die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1176355#post1176355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Wheaton, while only having a much smaller range of rolls to work with (as he only guest'd in two episodes of CR), still rolled disproportionately lower than would be statistically expected overall for his rolls and very much rolled more nat-1s than he &amp;quot;should&amp;quot; have, again per CRStats. So there's *some* legitimacy to his &amp;quot;curse&amp;quot;... lol (Similarly, on other shows he's guested on for G&amp;S, he rolls &amp;quot;badly&amp;quot; for &amp;quot;x&amp;quot;, regardless of the dice/numbers involved -- such as when he played with Matt Mercer, Ivan van Norman and others in a Paranoia game (where low is good and high is bad)... and instead of having disproportionately low rolls (1s, and 1-10s), he rolled high (including several 16-20s, more than he &amp;quot;should&amp;quot; have&amp;quot;... so yeah: there's *something* to the Wheaton Dice Curse(tm)... )</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s something to the idea that, on camera, Wheaton has rolled poorly with disproportionate frequency. I believe that something is coincidence, combined with a healthy dose of cognitive bias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1176355#post1176355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah -- that was sad/unfortunate. (However, even before the stream had started, Orion had most often been &amp;quot;problematic&amp;quot; and a touch of a pwrgmr in their home-PF game, per Liam's comments and some others. It was manageable, though, and usually not too out of line until the stream got going and Orion's personal issues became... well... <i>issues</i>... ) He and Matt had a friendly-enough encounter a few months ago at some place (with Sam, if I recall correctly), and he/they posted a couple pics of it on Twitter/whatnot, so there's at least a civility in place. (Matt has said at numerous conventions, when the subject of Orion would be brought up, that he genuinely wishes him well and that they are not enemies or anything like that... just sometimes people go on different paths in life and all you can do is wish them well.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh -- apparently (as I just went to check), Orion has taken down all of his Draconian Knights vids/audios/what-have-you, as well as has at least temporarily terminated his Twitch channel, as of a day or two ago. Hope everything is good for him, or at least heading in a good direction... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely hope things are going ok for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T06:27:49-08:00","id":1176503,"title":"","content":"So, what do you people think of the new crew? I personally am liking all the new characters although I wish Liam tried to do something other than mopey down on his luck characters for once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T09:14:21-08:00","id":1176530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1176503#post1176503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what do you people think of the new crew? I personally am liking all the new characters although I wish Liam tried to do something other than mopey down on his luck characters for once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love them. Mollymauk is my favorite. Sexy tiefling fortune teller with an Irish accent? Yes, please. Though it would have been nice to see him try a non-homebrew class for a change. I also like Jester a lot (I have a thing for horns), and seeing the two of them flirting was pretty great. I think Sam made the boldest character choice with Nott, which I appreciate. Also interesting that my three favorites were the three who decided to do non-American accents. Conversely, Liam\u2019s voice for Caleb is exactly the same as his voice for Vax. I\u2019ve also heard that exact same voice in a handful of video games, I wonder if he doesn\u2019t have much range. Travis went with another big buff intimidating guy, and his voice is pretty similar to Grog\u2019s, but I do like that Fjord is smarter than Grog. I like Beau a lot. Yasha is fine, but I\u2019m not a big fan of Aasimar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T10:04:15-08:00","id":1176795,"title":"","content":"I think despite both being traditionally tough races and having a deep, gruff voice I appreciate the differences more between Grog the Goliath and Fjord the Half-orc. Totally agree that is great to see him playing a character at least as smart as he is. Also loving Sam playing the shitiest Charisma character ever, what was it? a 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:40:06-08:00","id":1177054,"title":"","content":"So I never got into the original campaign, but I started the new season because of all the buzz and I\u2019m pleasantly surprised so far. Might stick with it!<br /> <br /> Definitely loving Yasha the most so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 01-18-2018, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T16:25:54-08:00","id":1177081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1176530#post1176530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love them. Mollymauk is my favorite. Sexy tiefling fortune teller with an Irish accent? Yes, please. Though it would have been nice to see him try a non-homebrew class for a change. I also like Jester a lot (I have a thing for horns), and seeing the two of them flirting was pretty great. I think Sam made the boldest character choice with Nott, which I appreciate. Also interesting that my three favorites were the three who decided to do non-American accents. Conversely, Liam\u2019s voice for Caleb is exactly the same as his voice for Vax. I\u2019ve also heard that exact same voice in a handful of video games, I wonder if he doesn\u2019t have much range. Travis went with another big buff intimidating guy, and his voice is pretty similar to Grog\u2019s, but I do like that Fjord is smarter than Grog. I like Beau a lot. Yasha is fine, but I\u2019m not a big fan of Aasimar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah -- I like Molly, too, and Jester (as I said further up, though, Laura has a slight advantage because she played Jester in another game and has had her &quot;worked out&quot; as a character for over a year, so she's the most contextually solid of the group). Liam's accent fluctuated subtly -- it was a bit of Vax, but here and there with dips/shifts -- as he, much like Travis, is trying to find the &quot;root&quot; of the character. (Of everybody, Travis -- per Talks Machina -- is the least ready, as it were, for Fjord, but will almost certainly stabilize over the next few episodes.)<br /> <br /> Sam playing a goblin girl with a Chr:5 is nothing less than the perfect choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (S/he is my initial favorite, with Laura/Jester a close second; that will likely level out over time as people get more into their characters.) The character I like the least, though, is Beau -- nothing against Marisha, as she gets enough grief from a vocal minority in the fandom, but of them all it's Beau who feels the most &quot;forced&quot;/not-quite-&quot;there&quot; yet, even more so than Liam/Caleb's still-Vax-ish accent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:21:27-08:00","id":1178229,"title":"","content":"I had always wanted but never managed to check on Critical Role's first campaign. With the second one, I had to occasion to jump on board without having to recover past episodes.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm part of the fandom now. It's been fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-22-2018, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:05:46-08:00","id":1178545,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like that there is an easier starting point for new fans, since there is no previous experience required although there's still little easter eggs and call backs for the long time fans (loving trinkets and not being a fan of ale)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:27:19-08:00","id":1178551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1178545#post1178545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I like that there is an easier starting point for new fans, since there is no previous experience required although there's still little easter eggs and call backs for the long time fans (loving trinkets and not being a fan of ale)</div> </div> </div> </div>If life allows, I'm eventually going back to recover the first game, but yes, the idea of jumping in while being hundreds of hours behind is what always stopped me so far. The new campaign was the perfect excuse and I hope that someday I'll manage to say &quot;ooooh, that why they kept saying that&quot;<br /> <br /> Having said that, I do like the characters and it's clear they all really passionate about the game. A group of professionals giving free performances while having a good times is a nice bonus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:43:19-08:00","id":1178558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1178229#post1178229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had always wanted but never managed to check on Critical Role's first campaign. With the second one, I had to occasion to jump on board without having to recover past episodes.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm part of the fandom now. It's been fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same boat and loving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T13:54:18-08:00","id":1182372,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m kinda heartbroken; I didn\u2019t realize Yasha\u2019s player can only attend sparingly, and she was the character I was most curious about in episode one. Hope she can get to the table more.<br /> <br /> Loving this entire party, though. Super curious to see what Fjord and Caleb might be hiding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:20:28-08:00","id":1182385,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah. Ashley's work on Blindspot also made her more like a recurring guest start at times although there were periods of her playing for several episodes straigth back in the first campaign with Vox Machina. Don't despair, you will definitely see more of her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:35:09-08:00","id":1182979,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really in love with this entire cast. The only character in the party I dislike is Beau, and that might be because her player is the host of the annoying internal TV show we run on loop at work.<br /> <br /> Nott and Fjord\u2019s \u201cyeehaw\u201d moment in episode 4 made me lose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T11:00:50-08:00","id":1182984,"title":"","content":"I am still watching the second part of episode 4 (I try to dosify them) and currently at the Beau solo. Definitely kind of a dick, which is a far cry from her last character. Same with Caleb which at first seemed a re-do of some Vax mannerisms, but turned out to be completely different from what I initially thought. And Nott, Jester and Fjord... what can I say? They are all made of pure awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:08:31-08:00","id":1185381,"title":"","content":"I've been watching Critical Role since the first episode of the first campaign and have seen the first campaign twice now. I have an alpha subscription and nerdy CR merch. That's a lot of investment so I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> I see a few pros and cons in this new campaign, though, but nothing too major, and nothing that's not subject to change:<br /> <br /> + I love the new setting and I love the fact that they are low level. <br /> + Ashley: I like the way Ashley plays Yasha.<br /> + Taliesin: I like the visual design of Mollymauk.<br /> + Liam: Mostly a delight. I like Caleb as a character. I like the fact that he's a coward.<br /> + Sam: Originally apphrensive of a goblin character, but if anyone can pull it off it's Sam. I have enjoyed Nott so far.<br /> + Laura: I think Jester is a fun take on Clerics.<br /> + Travis: Fjord is my favorite character. I like every aspect of him and the way he is portrayed. <br /> <br /> - I was looking forward to see a young and ambitious group of adventurers and am a bit apprehensive of their immediate thrust into questionable moral character.<br /> - Ashley: Sometimes I wonder if the show would be better without Ashley in it (because she's barely in it). But it's Ashley. I want her to be in it. It just bothers me that she's not there.<br /> - Taliesin: I wonder if he only wants to make niche characters who are a bit emo. Not sure about him using a homebrewed class.<br /> - Marisha: I don't like Beau. I enjoyed her training scene and she may get more interesting down the line, but I really really don't like her right now. It's all in the attitude. <br /> - Liam: I would have wanted to see him play a more joyful character. Sometimes it gets cringey when he goes all-in on the intensity and is up in people's faces with emotional roleplay. Some of that is fine, but Vax was all about that. I fear that Caleb may go into that direction as well, but I hope that Nott is a good comedic balance for him to lighten up the mood.<br /> - Laura: I'm getting a bit too much of Jester. Her trickster nature feels like the biggest threat to the group at the moment, and I fear that unless she tones it down, I'm going to get sick of it. <br /> <br /> Those are my pros and cons of the new campaign. Now I'm trying to get through Court of Swords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T16:52:16-08:00","id":1185405,"title":"","content":"I only recently realized that sam\u2019s character is Nott, a goblin girl, who poses as not a goblin girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:50:02-08:00","id":1186447,"title":"","content":"My thoughts: I've seen the bulk of the first campaign (only missing a little bit from the middle episodes) and it got really good at the end as the game ramped up. So I am super psyched for the new campaign. I'm currently up to date thanks to Project Alpha (having watched all of the episodes to date as well as all of the Talks Machina) so here goes...<br /> <br /> Ashley: Like many of you I wish we could get more of her because I feel her character needs more exposure. But from what I've seen so far I like Yasha and LOVE her look.<br /> <br /> Laura: Hands down my favorite. I love Jester and I like how she just kind of flows from each interaction to the next with her goofy, yet sincere comments. And I like how inviting she eventually became toward Caleb and Nott. Her bubbly comments like &quot;Don't be a baaaaaaybeeee&quot; and &quot;stinkydoodie&quot; make me chuckle every time. Her ideas that went into the art make Jester cute as a button.<br /> <br /> Talisen: I like Mollymauk but I feel like I'm expecting more. He has this absolutely amazing look (far better in my opinion than any of the others) but his hesitancy to really explore an Irish accent has me mildly concerned. I know Matt and the others have indicated recently that some of the members may be using this as a way to help expand their vocal abilities so I suspect this is probably his hold up. He's waiting to spring it when he feels more comfortable. I also think that since his partner coming into the game was Ashley and she cannot make most games that this has limited some of his character's beginning growth/interactions. This will likely change.<br /> <br /> Sam: I was &quot;meh&quot; about Sam playing a character from another gender and I can see it still throws the other players off occasionally but I am loving poor Nott's foiables. He's playing her like she's a tiny version of the Hulk but instead of rage it's maddening complusions and the interactions between Caleb and Nott have been great. I like the fact that it's a human and a goblin of all things against the world. Their loyalty to one another really stands out.<br /> <br /> Travis: The only downside I have right now is he isn't playing his Wisdom right now. Which is fine because there will be plenty of time later. As a pretty smart, charismatic guy with a low wisdom he should occasionally come up with a plan that sounds amazing but he fails to factor in some threat or variable (or dismisses it or some such). But otherwise I love Fjord and I like his take on meeting Caleb for the first time. Like finding a kindred spirit in magic sort of.<br /> <br /> Marisha: Beauregard is kind of meh right now. I suspect she's probably going to be on a slow burn for growth. She's also strikes me as similar to the character she played in Saga of Sundry: Madness except more drunk and not as meek.<br /> <br /> Liam: I had a hard time with Caleb initially because he reminded me SO much of his character from Saga of Sundry: Madness that he played just before this game began. But after the first episode when he started getting the accent he wanted down and had some more interaction with the other characters I enjoyed it much more. I found it hilarious that Laura just claimed he stank and he just went with it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Sycophant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:11:19-08:00","id":1186458,"title":"","content":"Beau is still irritating me. Fjord has been such a breakout star for me, especially with the mystery surrounding his backstory; a lot of the fandom are speculating that he isn't even really a half-orc, and the accent switch during his solo scene has me profoundly curious. Nott and Caleb have stolen my heart, which is kind of remarkable because I hate Chaotic Stupid thieves and most Wizards, and both are playing those in very unique ways. Molly I feel has an interesting story, but for now he scarcely seems to exist; I want him in the spotlight and generally doing more, because as it stands right now there's no reason the tiefling carnie with the flashy clothes and peacock tattoo should not be the character fading into the wallpaper. Jester somehow winds up just shy of annoying for me; her cutesy mannerisms are nice, but I grimaced so hard when she was fighting undead gnolls with a gigantic lollipop last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T17:51:36-08:00","id":1186494,"title":"","content":"I feel like I\u2019m the only person who really likes Beau.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T09:39:14-08:00","id":1186700,"title":"","content":"Beau looks good art wise but the character is taking longer to grow on me than most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Sycophant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:29:24-08:00","id":1186716,"title":"","content":"I really like her characterization. Nothing against those who don\u2019t like her as much, I just find it a little surprising how consistently I\u2019m hering people say she hasn\u2019t grown on them yet, while I really liked her from the first episode and still do. I love how butch she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:46:59-08:00","id":1186729,"title":"","content":"To put it into RPG terms (for me): Beau right now is attempting to use Bluff or Intimidate and has neither so she is constantly taking penalties for being untrained. She has a good look to her and it sounds like her character has a lot of fighting prowess. But right now all I see is stoner/drunk without Jackie Chan like charisma to sell it. This isn't to say she won't develop into something more and I have faith she can (since she's actually an actor).<br /> <br /> Side note without spoilers: the most recent episode has Taliesin branching out and doing more of an Irish accent so I'm happy to hear it's coming a long","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm