144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T00:51:50-07:00","id":1234558,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s one way to break a new studio in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T02:27:17-07:00","id":1234564,"title":"","content":"Can someone tell me what happened in the last episode? I usually get to those a few days later, but all I know for know is that Ashly Burch was there and that something &quot;bad&quot; happened. Now apparently some people are...throwing hate at her? That's what the Internet is saying, at least.<br /> <br /> I love Ashly, the thought there's one in a million chance I can ever meet her is one of the main really-stupid-yet-somehow-useful things I keep in mind to motivate me to self-improve. Got a rather serious crush for her and think she's great in general, so those news are not cool.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Obviously, nothing that happens in game is an excuse to harass people, but I'd like to understand the circumstances","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-13-2018, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T04:49:08-07:00","id":1234586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread#post1020797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I never really read D&amp;D so I only get the jist of the rules and the setting. So like a rating of 10 is average human in a trait? What is the in character explanation for the party after killing some goblins all of the sudden they know more spells and can cook or whatever. It feels to much like a videogame, I don't understand how powers even work in D&amp;D, most things are spells? I don't get how for instance Vex learns new ranger powers? Some people in the world just randomly have magic powers in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> They also seem to ignore that Tiberius had excellent Charisma, he shouldn't have been treated so much like a goof, and Percy tries to be a world class genius, but he chooses battle stats like Dexterity over Intelligence or Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, some people in the world of D&amp;D randomly have magic powers. They're called SORCERERS! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But 10 is considered to be the baseline average for a typical human, because you don't get any bonuses or negatives. For every 2 attribute points above 10, you get a +1, and for every 2 attribute points below 10, you get a -1 to your rolls. For every 4 levels you gain, you get to 1 extra attribute point to spend.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Rangers having magic, they are basically the Paladin counterpart of a Druid. They get access to 1st level Druid spells starting at level 4, just like how Paladins gain access to 1st level Cleric spells at level 4.<br /> <br /> Rangers are wardens of nature and protectors of the wilderness, so them acquiring spells later on is supposed to represent nature's gratitude by bestowing them with some extra power. Unfortunately, many interpretations of the D&amp;D Ranger throughout media have often forgotten about, or chose not to demonstrate their magical abilities and instead focus on how great at archery and swordplay they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-13-2018, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T07:16:06-07:00","id":1234626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1234564#post1234564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone tell me what happened in the last episode? I usually get to those a few days later, but all I know for know is that Ashly Burch was there and that something &amp;quot;bad&amp;quot; happened. Now apparently some people are...throwing hate at her? That's what the Internet is saying, at least.<br /> <br /> I love Ashly, the thought there's one in a million chance I can ever meet her is one of the main really-stupid-yet-somehow-useful things I keep in mind to motivate me to self-improve. Got a rather serious crush for her and think she's great in general, so those news are not cool.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Obviously, nothing that happens in game is an excuse to harass people, but I'd like to understand the circumstances</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t seen the episode yet, but I do know that<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mollymauk dies.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> If people are mad at Ashly Burch, it could be that they perceive it as being her fault somehow? Not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T07:25:46-07:00","id":1234628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1234626#post1234626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven\u2019t seen the episode yet, but I do know that<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Mollymauk dies.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> If people are mad at Ashly Burch, it could be that they perceive it as being her fault somehow? Not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that would explain what all this fuss is about. Thanks.<br /> <br /> From what I'm getting, most people seem to agree that it was tragic but still roleplayed well on both parts, but some vocal ones are mad at either Ashly or Matt for that. I'll have a clearer picture once I see the episode, but I doubt that toxic attitude is justified at all<br /> <br /> Gotta say that people on Tumblr and Twitter were good at avoiding spoilers: I knew something bad happened but not its exact nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:18:13-07:00","id":1234738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1234564#post1234564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone tell me what happened in the last episode? I usually get to those a few days later, but all I know for know is that Ashly Burch was there and that something &amp;quot;bad&amp;quot; happened. Now apparently some people are...throwing hate at her? That's what the Internet is saying, at least.<br /> <br /> I love Ashly, the thought there's one in a million chance I can ever meet her is one of the main really-stupid-yet-somehow-useful things I keep in mind to motivate me to self-improve. Got a rather serious crush for her and think she's great in general, so those news are not cool.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Obviously, nothing that happens in game is an excuse to harass people, but I'd like to understand the circumstances</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers ahead, obviously.<br /> <br /> The remaining members of the Nein are hunting the slavers that captured Fjord, Jester, and Yasha. Along the road, they find Ashly\u2019s character, a dwarf named Keg with a grudge against the slavers; it turns out she ised to be one of them. She warns them that they\u2019re a reall nasty bunch, and gonna be hard to take down in a fight - it\u2019ll be the five of them versus seven of the slavers. The Nein set up a pretty clever ambush, and the fight begins.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s where everything goes to hell.<br /> <br /> Nott is trying to unlock all of the slave cages, so she\u2019s not making any attacks on her turns. Keg is having a hard time closing into melee due to her speed and Ashly roleplaying her as terrified of these slavers; she gives herself Disadvantage on everything as part of her roleplay. This then leaves Molly, Beau, and Caleb to try and fight seven powerful enemies on their own, essentially.<br /> <br /> The entire party repeatedly rolled terribly on almost everything. Molly closed in on the boss slaver, got hit pretty bad, and then knocked himself unconscious spending his own HP on a Blood Maledict. The boss slaver then coup de grace\u2019d Molly, and let the others live as a warning to any others who mess with his crew.<br /> <br /> Folks are mad at Ashly for essentially taking herself out of combat. Folks are also mad at Taliesen for using an ability that costs his own HP when he had 4HP left. Folks are mad at Matt because they think a this fight was borderline unwinnable. Folks are mad at Sam for not contributing to the fight at all. Folks are really sad that Mollymauk is dead and not likely to come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:31:28-07:00","id":1234740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1020797-the-critical-role-thread?p=1234738#post1234738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoilers ahead, obviously.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Regina. That does explain a lot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:50:42-07:00","id":1234748,"title":"","content":"Yeesh. Yeah, I can see why folks would be mad about Ashly voluntarily giving herself Disadvantage for roleplay reasons. I myself am of the opinion that as a player, what your character \u201cwould do\u201d is entirely up to you, and as part of a cooperative game, it is common courtesy to roleplay your character in a way that what they \u201cwould do\u201d is what\u2019s good for the team. But I also recognize that not everyone plays or likes to play the same way I do, and I\u2019m certainly not going to get mad at someone for playing their character that way in someone else\u2019s table, particularly not one that is as much performance art as it is a game. Besides, by the sound of things, her not taking that disadvantage might well not have made enough of a difference anyway.<br /> <br /> As for Matt, I haven\u2019t seen the episode, but I\u2019d tend to give him the benefit of the doubt that if the fight was designed to be especially challenging, it was done with intention and the difficulty properly telegraphed.<br /> <br /> Nott trying to unlock the cages just makes sense. That seems like a tactically sound decision to me if their goal was to free the slaves, since they knew the fight was going to be difficult and they couldn\u2019t be sure they\u2019d win, making sure the slaves can get free even if they lose seems like the best decision.<br /> <br /> Talisen choosing to use an ability that sacrificed HP, while he was at low HP, against an enemy he knew hit very hard? That\u2019s a clear signal to me that he knew he was screwed anyway and wanted to make the best he could out of a bad situation. Sometimes sacrificing your own character for the good of the group is the best move you can make. This sounds like one of those times.<br /> <br /> Also, this is D&amp;D. Resurrection is a thing. Molly may not be gone for good, and even if he is, he gave us a great story in the time we had with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:58:14-07:00","id":1234750,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m in a weird spot where I\u2019m not upset at anyone for how things went and Molly is one of my least-favorite characters, but I\u2019ll still admit that a permanent loss and seeing how deflated everyone was definitely has been a huge downer. And I\u2019d be doing a lot worse if Caleb, Nott, or Fjord had died.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s hoping everyone is okay, the internet behaves, and Tal can make a character he loves just as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T15:45:38-07:00","id":1235736,"title":"","content":"I actually read this thread before I watched the episode in question and being a long term ST this is what I came away with: While I commend Ashly for wanting to play her character as she saw it, I felt it was a very bad on-the-fly decision and directly led to much of the scene falling apart. And had I been running the game I'd likely have a side conversation about being open with communications before game, and nothing this altering without giving the ST a heads up. Mostly because of the perceived fall out we are discussing (blame casting, etc). I just didn't feel her desire for revenge warranted such a drastic call unless the point of her joining was to ICly throw the fight yet look like she tried, giving the slavers a mole in what remained of their group.<br /> <br /> Granted no one can account for poor rolls so it's not like I would single her out, but of the various plans this group comes up with they did a pretty darn good job initially. And I feel if they had all committed to the act, they may have gotten somewhere. Even if it was a partial victory like freeing Yasha but the others were still trapped.<br /> <br /> Sam needed to attack and not sneak around the carts, especially with the warnings Ashly was giving IC. I see 'why' he was aiming for that but they seriously needed more damage output and 1 successful shot at the sorcerer who cast Dispel Magic would have been a huge boon in their favor. So to me that was a bad spot. Talisen trying to act as a tank instead of partnering up with Beau wasn't a sound move either, and seeing as his powers require him to use his own blood, that was a huge error on his part. Kudos to him for owning the error though at the end. I think that was exactly what happened. He stated an action, went through with it, and then realized he didn't have the HP to make it. But instead of retconning he followed through.<br /> <br /> But those are just my thoughts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Sycophant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T19:41:23-07:00","id":1236266,"title":"","content":"Tal confirmed on Talks Machina that he has rolled a new character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:18:56-07:00","id":1236416,"title":"","content":"Yup I saw that. I hope they do a clean split and let the character remain dead. I liked Molly a lot (mostly look wise) but something about this whole situation just feels like he needs to remain dead, as any attempt to bring him back would just cheapen what happened","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Sycophant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T10:30:46-07:00","id":1236470,"title":"","content":"News from Talks last night: Taliesen has rolled a new character, says Mollymauk is not the type to have ever come back as a ghost, Ashly is playing with them for three more sessions, EVERYONE cried more than once.<br /> <br /> ////<br /> <br /> I\u2019m afraid this makes me, like, needlessly cruel, but I\u2019ve seen a small but larger-than-expected number of folks saying they\u2019re quitting the show over this. Can someone help me grasp that mindset? Like, characters die in fiction, and they especially die in low-level D&amp;D. It\u2019s sad, sure, but I\u2019m not sure why someone would jump ship over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T12:47:12-07:00","id":1236517,"title":"","content":"It's because of the meta-aspect of the game. Standard fiction, especially Game of Thrones, has death fairly regularly. But it doesn't share the same co-op writing-playing aspect that RPGs have. So it seems people are upset because Ashly, as soon as the combat started, declared that she was going to take disadvantage for reasons people disagree with (and I do as well).<br /> <br /> Now I've haven't followed any of the recent discourse, but it sounds like the reason people are leaving is partly because they were/are passionate about the game show and Ashly's initial role in it and how CR has handled it.<br /> <br /> I personally felt she made a very split second call prior to a major event, and that bad judgment call helped stir the anger fans had. And in that I agree with them. She wasn't however the only reason the scene quickly fell apart and it shouldn't be placed on her shoulders like that and it isn't reason enough to quit watching, but for some apparently it is. Passionate fans are going to respond passionately, and CR is kidding themselves if they think people sit through 4 hour episodes weekly are going to sit quietly to something they perceive as some kind of injustice. Especially when they see real tears.<br /> <br /> Marisha's comments on Twitter (or where ever she made them) calling down this group for being angry and lashing out was also poor choice. They have been in this scene now since 2015, and if they haven't learned yet to not feed the trolls they never will. Brian's snarky comments from time to time on Talks Machina don't help matters either.<br /> <br /> They don't have to virtue signal, protect, or otherwise make any sort of reference to passionate fans who are handling this poorly. If said fan can't get a grip they will wind up being banned, blocked, or with some other punitive measure taken against them. It was a mistake, but you don't solve a mistake by making more of them and it seems both CR and the passionate show quitters need to learn that.<br /> <br /> I'm betting there are some of these show quitters who secretly don't know how to handle negativity and/or express themselves and are secretly waiting to see what happens next. Ashly may have made a very bad decision but it wasn't just her. And the CR cast will need her to help carry the show for a bit with 3 of the main stars being out and possibly 4 depending on how the story goes and when they can insert Talesin back IC. And if they give it half a chance with the next episode I think we'll see some amazing, in depth scenes<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Star Wars: the Fractured Galaxy (WEG) Bi Weekly Wed 7pm <br /> Modern Age Heroes (MSHRPG) Bi Weekly Sat 6pm <br /> Mythic Savannah (WOD mixed genre) Bi Weekly Fri 7:30pm<br /> Kingdoms of the Shattered Crown (D&amp;D 5e) Bi Weekly Thur 7:30pm<br /> <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.twitch.tv/losttribesgaming</a> (all listings are AZ time: PST/MST)","edited":{"userid":21138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","user":"Sycophant","date":". 07-18-2018, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21138-sycophant","name":"Syc